<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How AI Amigos browser tools, local storage, exports, analytics, and feed retrieval protect visitor inputs."><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy by architecture</p><h1>Your tool inputs stay on your device.</h1><p>The five workbench tools run entirely in the browser. AI Amigos does not receive the values you enter or the outputs generated from them.</p><h2>Local storage</h2><p>A versioned result may be saved in your browser so you can return to it. Use each tool’s Reset action to remove that local copy. Clearing site data in your browser also removes it.</p><h2>Exports and sharing</h2><p>Markdown, JSON, CSV, copy, and print happen only when you choose them. “Share this tool” copies a stable tool page link and never adds your inputs or result to the URL.</p><h2>Anonymous measurement</h2><p>Umami is inactive unless a verified site ID is configured. If enabled, AI Amigos sends only an anonymous event name and resource ID—for example, tool completion or template copy. Form fields and generated outputs are never included.</p><h2>News feeds</h2><p>Approved RSS or Atom sources are retrieved during the site build, not by your browser. Only sanitized metadata and original links are displayed. A source without a valid response or cached snapshot fails closed.</p><h2>Newsletter and contact</h2><p>Subscription collection is inactive until a provider and matching retention notice are configured. Contact actions open your email application; AI Amigos does not host a contact-form database.</p><h2>External destinations</h2><p>External source, newsletter, and newspaper links have their own privacy terms. Review them before entering information.</p></div></BaseLayout>
